## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical skills in designing a multi-tenant, event-driven API on GCP using API Gateway, Cloud Tasks, and Cloud Run, with per-tenant isolation and observable patterns. It focuses on real components, trade-offs, and testability.

## Key Concepts
- API Gateway
- Cloud Tasks
- Cloud Run
- per-tenant isolation (buckets and service accounts)
- idempotent processing
- observability (Cloud Logging/Monitoring)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo dedupe check against Firestore
async function isDuplicate(eventId, tenantId) {
  const doc = await Firestore.collection('dedup').doc(`${tenantId}_${eventId}`).get();
  if (doc.exists) return true;
  await Firestore.collection('dedup').doc(`${tenantId}_${eventId}`).set({ seenAt: Date.now() });
  return false;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test idempotency and failure paths end-to-end?
- How would you monitor and alert on retries or quota exhaustion in Cloud Tasks?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical multi-tenant data isolation, cross-project access, and production-grade analytics pipelines with Dataflow, Vertex AI, and GCS, plus governance controls.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation with per-tenant buckets and datasets
- Signed URL validation, secure data ingestion
- Dataflow pipelines with per-tenant routing
- Vertex AI training orchestration and guardrails
- IAM least privilege, VPC Service Controls, data residency
- Audit logging and correlation IDs

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Cloud Function snippet for validating signed uploads
exports.validateSignedUrl = (req, res) => {
  const { signature, tenantId } = req.query;
  if (!signature || !tenantId) return res.status(400).send('Invalid');
  // Real systems verify HMAC with tenant secret from Secret Manager
  res.status(200).send('ok');
}
```

